@lang en
IMPORT `bmfire-indemnity`

-- The top-level decision: is a claim covered, which losses in it are, why not, and how
-- much Bao Minh pays. Every reason is named for the clause that gives it, so an answer
-- traces back to the Rules. Nothing in this module adds to the Rules; it puts the other
-- modules' booleans in the order the Rules raise them.
--
-- TWO LEVELS. Some bars take the whole claim away (the period, the premium, the
-- conditions, a general exclusion triggered by the incident). Others take one claimed loss
-- out and leave the rest (an item not in the Summary, a head of loss not insured, an
-- item-level exclusion, the risk's own exclusions where they depend on the item).

§ `The claim`

§§ `Why a claim, or a loss, is not covered`

DECLARE `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- the whole claim
    `preamble — the DAMAGE did not occur during the period of insurance`
    `preamble — the risk claimed under is not stated in the Policy Summary`
    `II.E — risk E is stated without risk D`
    `III.1(a)(i) — riot, civil commotion, strike or lockout, risk D not insured`
    `III.1(a)(ii) — war, invasion, foreign enemy, hostilities, civil war`
    `III.1(a)(iii) — rebellion, mutiny, rising, insurrection, revolution, riot, coup, martial law`
    `III.1(b)(i) — nuclear weapons material`
    `III.1(b)(ii) — ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or waste`
    `III.1(d) — pollution or contamination`
    `VI.2 — the policy is void for misdeclaration or non-disclosure`
    `VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost`
    `VI.5 — a warranty was not complied with`
    `VI.6 — the property was not kept in good repair, or DAMAGE not guarded against`
    `VII.1(a)(i) — no steps taken at once to minimise the loss`
    `VII.1(a)(ii) — Bao Minh not notified in writing at once`
    `VII.1(a)(iii) — the police not notified at once`
    `VII.1(b) — the written claim was not delivered in time`
    `VII.1 — the information and documents required were not supplied`
    `VII.2(a) — fraud, or a wilful act or connivance of the Insured`
    `VII.3 — the plans and information to repair or replace were not supplied`
    `VII.7 — the steps required against third parties were not taken`
    `VIII.3.2 — the cover was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`
    `VIII.3.2 — an endorsement relied on was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`
    -- one claimed loss
    `preamble — the property is not stated in the Policy Summary`
    `I — the loss was not at an insured location`
    `preamble — a head of loss the policy does not insure`
    `preamble — theft is not a risk in Section II`
    `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
    `II.A(a) — earthquake, volcano or another convulsion of nature`
    `II.A(b)(i) — the property's own fermentation, heating or spontaneous burning`
    `II.A(b)(ii) — the property undergoing a drying process or a process using heat`
    `II.A(b)(iii) — the property burned by order of a public authority`
    `II.A(b)(iv) — fire from an underground fire`
    `II.A(c) — forest, bush, grassland, wilderness or jungle fire, or burning land to clear it`
    `II.A — explosion of a domestic boiler or gas, from an earthquake, volcano or convulsion of nature`
    `II.B(a) — the pressure vessel that exploded, or its internal parts`
    `II.B(b) — Terrorism by persons acting for an organisation`
    `II.D.1(a) — Terrorism by persons acting for an organisation`
    `II.D.1(b) — civil commotion that is part of, or grows into, a popular uprising`
    `II.D.1(c) — a malicious act, other than a wilful act of strikers, demonstrators or locked-out workers`
    `II.D.1(d) — malicious erasure or corruption of information on a computer system`
    `II.D.2(a) — consequential or indirect loss`
    `II.D.2(b) — stopping or interrupting work, a process or an operation`
    `II.D.2(c) — dispossession by confiscation or requisition`
    `II.D.2(d) — dispossession of a building by unlawful occupation`
    `II.E — DAMAGE caused by theft or attempted theft`
    `II.G(i)(a) — water overflowing from a water source, reservoir, canal, dam, apparatus or pipe`
    `II.G(i)(b) — a flood from the sea`
    `II.G(ii) and II.H(i) — frost, subsidence or landslip`
    `II.G(iii) and II.H(ii) — awnings, signboards, outside fixtures, gates, fences, property in the open`
    `II.G(iv) and II.H(iii) — a building under works, its openings not completed against storm`
    `II.G(v) — water or rain, unless it came in through an opening the storm made`
    `II.H(iv) — rain, unless it came in through an opening the storm made`
    `II.H(v) — water overflowing from a water tank, apparatus or pipe`
    `II.I(i) — leakage or discharge from an automatic sprinkler installation`
    `II.I(ii) — DAMAGE to a building left empty or not in use`
    `III.1(c) — electrical machinery damaged by its own electrical fault`
    `III.2(a) — property of a named category, not recorded as insured`
    `III.3 — consequential loss`
    `III.4 — theft or robbery during or after a fire`
    `VIII.1(a)(i) — electronic data, or loss of use or cost from it`
    `VIII.2 Part 1 — a date change contributed`
    `VIII.2 Part 2 — cost of altering or modifying a computer system`

-- `only if` condition reason: the reason, in a list of one, where the condition holds.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
      r IS A `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`only if` b r MEANS
    IF b THEN LIST r ELSE EMPTY

§§ `Reasons the whole claim fails`

-- In the order the Rules raise them: preamble, II.E, III, VI, VII, VIII.3.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons the whole claim fails` c MEANS
  concat (LIST
    `only if` (NOT (`preamble — the DAMAGE occurred during the period of insurance` (c's `Policy Summary`) (c's `date of the DAMAGE`)))
                  `preamble — the DAMAGE did not occur during the period of insurance`,
    `only if` (NOT (`preamble — the risk claimed under is stated in the Policy Summary` c))
                  `preamble — the risk claimed under is not stated in the Policy Summary`,
    `only if` (    c's `risk claimed under` EQUALS `E. malicious damage`
          AND NOT (`II.E — risk E is insured only together with risk D` (c's `Policy Summary`)))
                  `II.E — risk E is stated without risk D`,
    `only if` (`III.1(a)(i) — riot, civil commotion, strike or lockout, risk D not insured` c)
                  `III.1(a)(i) — riot, civil commotion, strike or lockout, risk D not insured`,
    `only if` (`III.1(a)(ii) — war, invasion, foreign enemy, hostilities, civil war` c)
                  `III.1(a)(ii) — war, invasion, foreign enemy, hostilities, civil war`,
    `only if` (`III.1(a)(iii) — rebellion, mutiny, rising, insurrection, revolution, riot, coup, martial law` c)
                  `III.1(a)(iii) — rebellion, mutiny, rising, insurrection, revolution, riot, coup, martial law`,
    `only if` (`III.1(b)(i) — nuclear weapons material` c)
                  `III.1(b)(i) — nuclear weapons material`,
    `only if` (`III.1(b)(ii) — ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or waste` c)
                  `III.1(b)(ii) — ionising radiation or radioactive contamination from nuclear fuel or waste`,
    `only if` (`III.1(d) — pollution or contamination, not from or causing an insured risk` c)
                  `III.1(d) — pollution or contamination`,
    `only if` (`VI.2 — Bao Minh treats the policy as void` (c's `conduct`))
                  `VI.2 — the policy is void for misdeclaration or non-disclosure`,
    `only if` (`VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost` c)
                  `VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost`,
    `only if` (`VI.5 — the claim is lost for a warranty not complied with` c)
                  `VI.5 — a warranty was not complied with`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VI.6 — met` (c's `conduct`)))
                  `VI.6 — the property was not kept in good repair, or DAMAGE not guarded against`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VII.1(a)(i) — met` c))
                  `VII.1(a)(i) — no steps taken at once to minimise the loss`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VII.1(a)(ii) — met` c))
                  `VII.1(a)(ii) — Bao Minh not notified in writing at once`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VII.1(a)(iii) — met` c))
                  `VII.1(a)(iii) — the police not notified at once`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VII.1(b) — the written claim was delivered in time` c))
                  `VII.1(b) — the written claim was not delivered in time`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VII.1, closing paragraph — met` c))
                  `VII.1 — the information and documents required were not supplied`,
    `only if` (`VII.2(a) — every benefit is forfeited` (c's `conduct`))
                  `VII.2(a) — fraud, or a wilful act or connivance of the Insured`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VII.3 — met` c))
                  `VII.3 — the plans and information to repair or replace were not supplied`,
    `only if` (NOT (`VII.7 — met` c))
                  `VII.7 — the steps required against third parties were not taken`,
    `only if` (`VIII.3.2 — the cover was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE` c)
                  `VIII.3.2 — the cover was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`,
    `only if` (`VIII.3.2 — an endorsement relied on was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE` c)
                  `VIII.3.2 — an endorsement relied on was cancelled for unpaid premium before the DAMAGE`)

§§ `Reasons one claimed loss is not covered`

-- The risk's own words and exclusions, for the risk claimed under. Empty when the risk
-- takes the loss in; the "not of the kind" reason when no limb of the risk describes the
-- incident; otherwise the risk's exclusions that apply.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
      l IS A `A claimed loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons under the risk claimed under` c l MEANS
  IF `II — the loss falls within the risk claimed under` c l
  THEN EMPTY
  ELSE CONSIDER c's `risk claimed under`
       WHEN `A. fire, lightning, and explosion of a domestic boiler or gas` THEN
         IF NOT (`II.A — some limb of risk A describes the incident` c)
         THEN LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
         ELSE concat (LIST
           `only if` (`II.A — fire, from explosion or any other cause` c AND `II.A(a) — earthquake, volcano or another convulsion of nature` c)
                         `II.A(a) — earthquake, volcano or another convulsion of nature`,
           `only if` (`II.A — fire, from explosion or any other cause` c AND `II.A(b)(i) — the property's own fermentation, heating or spontaneous burning` l)
                         `II.A(b)(i) — the property's own fermentation, heating or spontaneous burning`,
           `only if` (`II.A — fire, from explosion or any other cause` c AND `II.A(b)(ii) — the property undergoing a drying process or a process using heat` l)
                         `II.A(b)(ii) — the property undergoing a drying process or a process using heat`,
           `only if` (`II.A — fire, from explosion or any other cause` c AND `II.A(b)(iii) — the property burned by order of a public authority` l)
                         `II.A(b)(iii) — the property burned by order of a public authority`,
           `only if` (`II.A — fire, from explosion or any other cause` c AND `II.A(b)(iv) — fire from an underground fire` c)
                         `II.A(b)(iv) — fire from an underground fire`,
           `only if` (`II.A — fire, from explosion or any other cause` c AND `II.A(c) — forest, bush, grassland, wilderness or jungle fire, or burning land to clear it` c)
                         `II.A(c) — forest, bush, grassland, wilderness or jungle fire, or burning land to clear it`,
           `only if` (    `II.A — explosion of a boiler or of gas used for domestic purposes, where gas is not produced` c
                 AND `II.A — the explosion limb's exclusion of earthquake, volcanic eruption or another convulsion of nature` c)
                         `II.A — explosion of a domestic boiler or gas, from an earthquake, volcano or convulsion of nature`)
       WHEN `B. explosion` THEN
         IF NOT (`II.B — explosion` c)
         THEN LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
         ELSE concat (LIST
           `only if` (`II.B(a) — damage to the boiler, economiser, vessel, machine or apparatus under pressure that exploded, or its internal parts` l)
                         `II.B(a) — the pressure vessel that exploded, or its internal parts`,
           `only if` (`II.B(b) — Terrorism by persons acting for an organisation` c)
                         `II.B(b) — Terrorism by persons acting for an organisation`)
       WHEN `D. riot, strike and lockout` THEN
         IF NOT (`II.D — DAMAGE directly caused by any of (a) to (d)` c)
         THEN LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
         ELSE append (`only if` (`II.D.1(c) — a malicious act, other than a wilful act of strikers, demonstrators or locked-out workers` c)
                                    `II.D.1(c) — a malicious act, other than a wilful act of strikers, demonstrators or locked-out workers`)
                     (`the reasons under D's exclusions other than 1(c)` c l)
       WHEN `E. malicious damage` THEN
         IF NOT (`II.E — DAMAGE caused by a malicious act of any person` c)
         THEN LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
         ELSE append (`only if` (`II.E — DAMAGE caused by theft or attempted theft` l)
                                    `II.E — DAMAGE caused by theft or attempted theft`)
                     (`the reasons under D's exclusions other than 1(c)` c l)
       WHEN `G. storm and tempest` THEN
         IF NOT (`II.G — storm or tempest` c)
         THEN LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
         ELSE concat (LIST
           `only if` (`II.G(i)(a) — water overflowing from a natural or artificial water source, reservoir, canal, dam, or water apparatus or pipe` c)
                         `II.G(i)(a) — water overflowing from a water source, reservoir, canal, dam, apparatus or pipe`,
           `only if` (`II.G(i)(b) — a flood from the sea` c)
                         `II.G(i)(b) — a flood from the sea`,
           `only if` (`II.G(ii) and II.H(i) — frost, subsidence or landslip` c)
                         `II.G(ii) and II.H(i) — frost, subsidence or landslip`,
           `only if` (`II.G(iii) and II.H(ii) — awnings, blinds, signboards, outside fixtures, gates, fences and movable property in the open` l)
                         `II.G(iii) and II.H(ii) — awnings, signboards, outside fixtures, gates, fences, property in the open`,
           `only if` (`II.G(iv) and II.H(iii) — a building under construction, renovation or repair, its openings not completed against storm` l)
                         `II.G(iv) and II.H(iii) — a building under works, its openings not completed against storm`,
           `only if` (`II.G(v) — water or rain, unless it came in through an opening the storm made` l)
                         `II.G(v) — water or rain, unless it came in through an opening the storm made`)
       WHEN `H. storm, tempest and flood` THEN
         IF NOT (`II.H — storm, tempest or flood` c)
         THEN LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
         ELSE concat (LIST
           `only if` (`II.G(ii) and II.H(i) — frost, subsidence or landslip` c)
                         `II.G(ii) and II.H(i) — frost, subsidence or landslip`,
           `only if` (`II.G(iii) and II.H(ii) — awnings, blinds, signboards, outside fixtures, gates, fences and movable property in the open` l)
                         `II.G(iii) and II.H(ii) — awnings, signboards, outside fixtures, gates, fences, property in the open`,
           `only if` (`II.G(iv) and II.H(iii) — a building under construction, renovation or repair, its openings not completed against storm` l)
                         `II.G(iv) and II.H(iii) — a building under works, its openings not completed against storm`,
           `only if` (`II.H(iv) — rain, unless it came in through an opening the storm made` l)
                         `II.H(iv) — rain, unless it came in through an opening the storm made`,
           `only if` (`II.H(v) — water overflowing from a water tank, water apparatus or water pipe` c)
                         `II.H(v) — water overflowing from a water tank, apparatus or pipe`)
       WHEN `I. water from tanks, apparatus or pipes` THEN
         IF NOT (`II.I — water overflowing from a water tank, water apparatus or water pipe` c)
         THEN LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`
         ELSE concat (LIST
           `only if` (`II.I(i) — leakage or discharge from an automatic sprinkler installation` c)
                         `II.I(i) — leakage or discharge from an automatic sprinkler installation`,
           `only if` (`II.I(ii) — DAMAGE to a building left empty or not in use` l)
                         `II.I(ii) — DAMAGE to a building left empty or not in use`)
       -- C, F and J have no exclusion of their own: outside them is "not of the kind".
       OTHERWISE LIST `II — the incident is not of the kind the risk claimed under describes`

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
      l IS A `A claimed loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons under D's exclusions other than 1(c)` c l MEANS
  concat (LIST
    `only if` (`II.D.1(a) — Terrorism by persons acting for an organisation` c)
                  `II.D.1(a) — Terrorism by persons acting for an organisation`,
    `only if` (`II.D.1(b) — civil commotion that is part of, or grows into, a popular uprising` c)
                  `II.D.1(b) — civil commotion that is part of, or grows into, a popular uprising`,
    `only if` (`II.D.1(d) — malicious erasure, loss, distortion or corruption of information on a computer system` c)
                  `II.D.1(d) — malicious erasure or corruption of information on a computer system`,
    `only if` (`II.D.2(a) — loss of income, delay, loss of market, or other consequential or indirect loss` l)
                  `II.D.2(a) — consequential or indirect loss`,
    `only if` (`II.D.2(b) — DAMAGE from stopping or interrupting work, a process or an operation` l)
                  `II.D.2(b) — stopping or interrupting work, a process or an operation`,
    `only if` (`II.D.2(c) — DAMAGE from dispossession by confiscation or requisition by order of a lawful authority` c l)
                  `II.D.2(c) — dispossession by confiscation or requisition`,
    `only if` (`II.D.2(d) — DAMAGE from dispossession of a building by unlawful occupation` c l)
                  `II.D.2(d) — dispossession of a building by unlawful occupation`)

-- The insuring clause pays for loss "do các rủi ro được ghi trong Bản tóm lược hợp đồng bảo
-- hiểm gây ra" (caused by the risks stated). Theft is none of the risks. Two clauses name
-- it: E excludes DAMAGE by theft, and III.4 excludes theft during or after a fire, which
-- presupposes that such theft might otherwise be argued to fall under A. Under every other
-- risk, a loss by theft is simply not caused by the risk (fork F32).
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
      l IS A `A claimed loss`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`preamble — theft is not a cause the risk claimed under answers for` c l MEANS
        l's `caused by theft, robbery or attempted theft`
    AND NOT (c's `risk claimed under` EQUALS `A. fire, lightning, and explosion of a domestic boiler or gas`)
    AND NOT (c's `risk claimed under` EQUALS `E. malicious damage`)

-- All the reasons one claimed loss is out, in the Rules' order.
GIVEN c   IS A `The claim`
      loc IS A `The loss at one location`
      l   IS A `A claimed loss`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
`the reasons the loss is not covered` c loc l MEANS
  concat (LIST
    `only if` (NOT (`preamble — the property is stated in the Policy Summary` l))
                  `preamble — the property is not stated in the Policy Summary`,
    `only if` (NOT (loc's `an insured location stated in the Policy Summary`))
                  `I — the loss was not at an insured location`,
    `only if` (NOT (`preamble — a head of loss the policy insures` (c's `Policy Summary`) l))
                  `preamble — a head of loss the policy does not insure`,
    `only if` (`preamble — theft is not a cause the risk claimed under answers for` c l)
              `preamble — theft is not a risk in Section II`,
    `the reasons under the risk claimed under` c l,
    `only if` (`III.1(c) — electrical machinery damaged by its own over-running, short-circuit, self-heating, arcing or leakage` l)
                  `III.1(c) — electrical machinery damaged by its own electrical fault`,
    `only if` (`III.2(a) — property of a category named in III.2(a), not recorded as insured` l)
                  `III.2(a) — property of a named category, not recorded as insured`,
    `only if` (`III.3 — consequential loss, other than rent insured under this policy` (c's `Policy Summary`) l)
                  `III.3 — consequential loss`,
    `only if` (`III.4 — loss by theft or robbery during or after a fire` c l)
                  `III.4 — theft or robbery during or after a fire`,
    `only if` (`VIII.1(a)(i) — loss of or damage to electronic data, or loss of use or cost from it` l)
                  `VIII.1(a)(i) — electronic data, or loss of use or cost from it`,
    `only if` (`VIII.2 Part 1 — excludes the loss` c loc l)
                  `VIII.2 Part 1 — a date change contributed`,
    `only if` (`VIII.2 Part 2 — cost of altering or modifying a computer system` l)
                  `VIII.2 Part 2 — cost of altering or modifying a computer system`)

§§ `The assessment`

DECLARE `The assessment of a claimed loss` HAS
    `location`                  IS A STRING
    `item`                      IS A STRING
    `reasons it is not covered` IS A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`

DECLARE `The assessment of a claim` HAS
    `reasons the whole claim fails` IS A LIST OF `A reason a claim or a loss is not covered`
    `losses`                        IS A LIST OF `The assessment of a claimed loss`
    `amount payable`                IS A NUMBER

-- Each location, keeping only the losses that are covered.
GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `The loss at one location`
`the covered losses` c MEANS
    map (GIVEN loc YIELD `The loss at one location` WITH
                            `location`                                         IS loc's `location`
                            `an insured location stated in the Policy Summary` IS loc's `an insured location stated in the Policy Summary`
                            `claimed losses`                                   IS filter (GIVEN l YIELD null (`the reasons the loss is not covered` c loc l)) (loc's `claimed losses`))
        (c's `losses`)

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable` c MEANS
    IF   null (`the reasons the whole claim fails` c)
    THEN `the amount payable on the covered losses` c (`the covered losses` c)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN c IS A `The claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `The assessment of a claimed loss`
`the assessment of each loss` c MEANS
    concat (map (GIVEN loc YIELD
                    map (GIVEN l YIELD `The assessment of a claimed loss` WITH
                                         `location`                  IS loc's `location`
                                         `item`                      IS l's `item`'s `description`
                                         `reasons it is not covered` IS `the reasons the loss is not covered` c loc l)
                        (loc's `claimed losses`))
                (c's `losses`))

@export Assess a claim under Bao Minh's fire and special perils rules: whether it is covered, which losses are out and why (each reason names its clause), and the amount Bao Minh pays in VND
GIVEN c IS A `The claim` @desc the claim: the Policy Summary, the risk claimed under, the date of the DAMAGE, the facts of the incident, the losses by location, the premium, changes, warranties and the Insured's conduct
GIVETH A `The assessment of a claim`
`the assessment of the claim` c MEANS
    `The assessment of a claim` WITH
        `reasons the whole claim fails` IS `the reasons the whole claim fails` c
        `losses`                        IS `the assessment of each loss` c
        `amount payable`                IS `the amount payable` c
